<title>FRANCE: Allied venture signs $100 mln engine deal.</title>
<headline>Allied venture signs $100 mln engine deal.</headline>
<dateline>LE BOURGET, France 1997-06-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The light helicopter engine venture of Allied Signal Aerospace and Rolls Royce unit Allison Engine Co. said on Saturday it signed an agreement valued at $100 million to deliver 100 engine packages to Ayres Corp.</p>
<p>The venture, the Light Helicopter Turbine Engine Co., said in a statement at the Paris Airshow that deliveries of the 100 shipsets of T800 engines for the Ayres Loadmaster would begin in May 1999.</p>
<p>It also said Federal Express had placed an initial order for 50 engine systems with options for 200 more, with deliveries set to begin in December 1999.</p>
<p>-- Le Bourget Newsroom, +33-1 41693650</p>
</text>
